<title>NETHERLANDS: BolsWessanen buys Hillsdown unit.</title>
<headline>BolsWessanen buys Hillsdown unit.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch food and drinks group BolsWessanen NV said on Tuesday it had acquired cereals firm Barber Chestergate from Hillsdown Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>BolsWessanen said it would pay an undisclosed cash sum for Barber Chestergate which has annual sales worth some 30 million guilders ($17.2 million) and employs 130 people.</p>
<p>Barber Chestergate makes breakfast cereals sold under retailers' own private labels.</p>
<p>Bolswessanen already owns British cereals firm Dailycer UK and said its share of the British cereals market would rise as a result of the Barber acquisition to 12 percent from nine.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
<p>($ = 1.744 Dutch Guilders)</p>
